	title: 'Adjust settings with Left and Right',
	spec: 'In the shared terminal and web /config modal, Left decreases the selected integer by one and Right increases it by one, within the setting bounds. Left sets a boolean off and Right sets it on. Left and Right pick the previous and next option of a choice, stopping at the first and last. Arrows work the same while the search box holds text. Apply changes immediately through the existing /config command, keeping the modal open. At a bound or an already selected boolean value, send nothing. Plain arrows affect only integer, boolean and choice rows outside inline editing; text cursor movement, Enter/Space and modified keys retain their behavior. Show the shortcuts in the modal hint and document them in tasks/w4/forms.md.',
